From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kan Zhu <kanzhu@cs.washington.edu>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 09:40:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/18] alignment: record speculative request work and
 committed output progress

Port the extraction from the spec5 alignment branch onto this DFlash2 base. The
per-request speculative progress bookkeeping moves out of EngineCore into
vllm/v1/engine/alignment.py so the consumer side can load iteration_request_details
by path and check the producer against it without importing torch or vllm.

Three behavior changes come with it. output_tokens_before is now read from the
live request in scheduler.requests rather than the scheduler's cached count,
which can still hold an async placeholder for an earlier batch. Each progress
entry carries external_request_id (the internal eight-hex suffix stripped) and
request_finished_before. An emitted count above one with no drafted tokens is
rejected.

The iteration-logging test asserts the new contract and deliberately disagrees
the cached count (12) with the live committed count (9) to pin the first change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
